Noncollinear DeltaSpin force and stress regression
================================================

Test PW DeltaSpin with nspin=4 and nonparallel xyz constraints of magnitude
2 mu_B on each atom. The energy, force and stress comparisons include a
regression for the onsite stress sign.

This test checks the energy, force and stress after both the charge density
and the constrained atomic magnetic moments converge to 1e-8. It retains
Davidson-subspace as the default solver, kpar=2 and the original structure,
pseudopotential, orbital basis, cutoff, smearing and mixing settings.

The previous charge threshold of 1e-6 and magnetic-moment threshold of 1e-4
stopped after 11 SCF steps. Its force and stress depended on the solver's
SCF trajectory more strongly than the existing reference tolerances allow.
The revised inputs tighten both convergence targets, set the initial
diagonalization threshold to 1e-10, disable empty-band threshold smoothing,
and increase the iteration budgets. The adaptive diagonalization threshold
remains enabled; pw_diag_thr_max is not set.

Reference provenance (2026-10-26)
-------------------------------
The reference uses Davidson-subspace output from a GNU 12.3 / OpenMPI 5.0.10
Release build with four MPI ranks and one OpenMP/BLAS thread. The build is
based on 77f7b4af69934064aa5f4b84267343e9135bc348 plus the accompanying
local PPCG/Davidson and threshold-control fixes. Binary SHA-256:
d9d2914b9f8f793d0da52f28b09a6996ae39483958658dfb72490f51c2b842f1.

Independent PPCG and CG runs used identical inputs except ks_solver.
PPCG and Davidson-subspace converged in 25 SCF steps, CG in 26. Their final
charge errors were 7.45e-9, 7.51e-9 and 8.78e-9; complete-space magnetic
moment RMS errors were 2.52e-9, 2.82e-9 and 7.21e-9 Bohr magnetons.
The final printed atomic moments independently satisfy the same target.

Maximum differences across all three solver pairs:
  total energy:             7.79e-9 eV
  force absolute-value sum:  6.0e-6 eV/Angstrom
  stress absolute-value sum: 2.50e-4 kbar
  individual force entry:   3.22e-7 eV/Angstrom
  individual stress entry:  9.03e-5 kbar

The original reference-check tolerances remain 1e-7 eV, 1e-4 eV/Angstrom
and 1e-3 kbar. The reference contains the same four properties as before;
timing output is not used as a numerical reference. All three tightened
calculations differ from the old stress reference by about 3.091 kbar in
the absolute-value sum, establishing the need for the reference update.
